YouTube channel REWA Technology today shared one of the first <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PHiZb9rMhmI">iPhone 18 Pro teardown videos</a>, offering a look inside the new device.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iPhone-18-Pro-Dynamic-Island-1.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1066090" /><br/>
iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max feature a smaller Dynamic Island, which Apple achieved by moving Face ID's infrared camera under the display in the top-left corner. The pixels above the infrared camera have a special pattern that lets infrared light pass through, yet the screen looks completely normal at typical viewing angles.<br/>
<br/>
The teardown shows the repositioned infrared camera, plus other changes like the larger 48-megapixel main camera with variable aperture.<br/>
